The policy boilerplate in fsck_sysfs_audit_rules.conf is adapted from
`external/selinux/libsepol/tests/policies/test-neverallow/policy.conf` at
SELinux submodule commit `085c131ad1b984bfa8ffdafee7a976e9d89f403c`.
The fixture source and compiled policy are retained for testing only. The
relevant upstream libsepol license is at
`vendor/sepatch/external/selinux/libsepol/LICENSE` (LGPL-2.1-or-later).

`fsck_sysfs_allow_roundtrip.conf` is derived from
`fsck_sysfs_audit_rules.conf`; it preserves the policy boilerplate and uses
sibling `dir.search` audit rules to exercise the legacy verifier's aggregate
change result for the target `dir.read` allow.

Regenerate the binary with:
`checkpolicy -N -c 31 -o fsck_sysfs_audit_rules.policy fsck_sysfs_audit_rules.conf`
